spec: S06-06, S06-07, S06-12, S06-13, S38-02

`--json ?` lists every field of the ticket-06 verbs and exits without calling the server
(so it works with any profile, even `down`).

```console
$ annotary -p down member rename x y --json ?
handle name role grants disabled created id

$ annotary -p down member disable x --json ?
handle name role grants disabled created id

$ annotary -p down member enable x --json ?
handle name role grants disabled created id

$ annotary -p down member grant x notes read --json ?
handle name role grants disabled created id

$ annotary -p down member role x owner --json ?
handle name role grants disabled created id

$ annotary -p down token mint --json ?
token id member name expires created

$ annotary -p down token list --json ?
id member name created last_used expires status revoked

$ annotary -p down token revoke x --json ?
id member revoked name

$ annotary -p down login --json ?
profile server handle role config

$ annotary -p down logout --json ?
profile handle revoked config

$ annotary -p down profile list --json ?
name server member role vault has_token

$ annotary -p down profile add x --json ?
name server vault has_token config

$ annotary -p down profile remove x --json ?
name server vault has_token config

$ annotary -p down profile default --json ?
? 1
error: unrecognized subcommand 'default'

Usage: annotary profile [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

For more information, try '--help'.

```
